  "prefLabel": "Ins 203.03 Inquiry by Hearing Officer",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 203.03 Inquiry by Hearing Officer. The hearing officer in an adjudicative proceeding shall question witnesses and make such inquiry of witnesses, parties, or counsel as the hearing officer believes appropriate to promote the fair, accurate, and efficient resolution of issues pending before the department.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Ins 200) #13073-A, eff 7-27-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins200.html"
